    <h2>Sentiment-Rating Divergence &amp; Sarcasm Detection</h2>
  </div>

  <p>A <strong>mismatch</strong> is defined as a review where the VADER polarity and star rating send conflicting signals: a high-star review (4–5 stars) with a clearly negative polarity (&lt;−0.05), or a low-star review (1–2 stars) with a clearly positive polarity (&gt;+0.05). These cases signal sarcasm, mixed-emotion reviews, or Unicode text that VADER misclassified.</p>

