<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ SECTION 6 — RECOMMENDATIONS -->
<section class="section" id="recommendations">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">6</div>
    <h2>Strategic Recommendations</h2>
  </div>

  <p>Prioritized recommendations for product strategy, derived directly from the data findings above. Ordered by estimated impact and urgency.</p>

  <div class="rec-grid">
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">Priority 1 — Pricing &amp; Monetization</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Reduce Subscription Friction for Claude &amp; Perplexity</div>
      <div class="rec-body">Claude (7.99%) and Perplexity (7.48%) lead all apps in pricing complaints. These are the highest thumbs-up earning complaint type (4.98 avg), meaning pricing frustrations resonate widely. Evaluate tiered freemium structures, usage-based billing options, or clearer paywall messaging. Given Bugs/Performance complaints also peak for Claude, address pricing <em>and</em> stability together to avoid a compounding churn signal.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">Priority 2 — Product Quality</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Accelerate Stability Roadmap for Claude &amp; Gemini</div>
      <div class="rec-body">Claude (5.54%) and Google Gemini (5.21%) lead in Bugs/Performance complaints. Bug reviews attract the highest community endorsement (6.91 avg thumbs-up), signaling that stability issues have outsized visibility. Mobile app crash patterns, slow load times, and feature regressions should be first-order engineering priorities, as this complaint type is most "contagious" in terms of peer amplification.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">Priority 3 — Accuracy / Trust</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Target Hallucination Reduction at Perplexity &amp; ChatGPT</div>
      <div class="rec-body">Perplexity (6.43%) and ChatGPT (5.45%) lead in Accuracy/Logic complaints — a core product differentiation issue. For a search-augmented tool like Perplexity, accuracy failures are especially damaging. Consider citation improvements, confidence indicators, and user-facing "verify this" controls. Accurate AI is a competitive moat: accuracy complaints are 3× harder to fix than bugs but create lasting brand damage when unaddressed.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">Priority 4 — Satisfaction Gap</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Study Copilot's UX Playbook</div>
      <div class="rec-body">Microsoft Copilot's lead is structurally large: 4.24 stars vs. the 3.45–3.81 range for all others, and the lowest complaint rate (9.72% total flagged). This likely reflects integration with Microsoft 365 (embedded workflow context), a narrower but more satisfied user base, and potentially better onboarding. Product teams should map the specific friction points where users drop from "satisfied" to "frustrated" for their own app vs. Copilot's known workflow-integrated design.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">Priority 5 — Analytics Infrastructure</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Move Beyond Star Ratings for Competitor Tracking</div>
      <div class="rec-body">A 12–14% mismatch rate for four of five apps means raw star averages systematically misrepresent user sentiment. Implement multi-signal competitive monitoring combining: VADER (or similar) NLP sentiment, theme tag distribution, review length trends, and thumbs-up velocity. A competitor's star rating going up while its mismatch rate rises is a warning sign, not a green light.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">Priority 6 — User Retention</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Mine Long-Form 2-Star Reviews for Churn Signals</div>
      <div class="rec-body">2-star reviews are the most verbose (38.2 avg words) and represent "almost churned" users: they cared enough to articulate specific reasons but didn't give up entirely. This cohort has the highest recovery potential. Build a qualitative review-reading program targeting 2-star reviews by theme to extract specific product improvement hypotheses. These users signal what would need to change to retain them — more signal-dense than 1-star rage-quits.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

